 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 542776,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "Suppose you have data that are normally distributed with mean 20 and standard deviation 6. Determine at what percentiles these data values fall: 25, 12, and 31.",
   "answers": [],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "free-response"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<p>80th</p>\n<p>9th</p>\n<p>97th</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>In an empty cell of Google Sheets, use the function NORM.DIST.</p>\n<p>NORM.DIST(your data value, your mean, your standard deviation, TRUE)</p>\n<p>For 25:</p>\n<p>Using your data: =NORM.DIST(25,20,6,TRUE)</p>\n<p>You will see the decimal version of the percentile: 0.79761619</p>\n<p>Convert the decimal to an approximate percentage: the 80<sup>th</sup> percentile</p>\n<p>For 12:</p>\n<p>Using your data: =NORM.DIST(12,20,6,TRUE)</p>\n<p>You will see the decimal version of the percentile: 0.09121121973</p>\n<p>Convert the decimal to an approximate percentage: the 9<sup>th</sup> percentile</p>\n<p>For 31:</p>\n<p>Using your data: =NORM.DIST(31,20,6,TRUE)</p>\n<p>You will see the decimal version of the percentile: 0.966234924</p>\n<p>Convert the decimal to an approximate percentage: the 97<sup>th</sup> percentile</p>"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
